          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Which form of protein-energy malnutrition is characterised by severe wasting yet</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which form of protein-energy malnutrition is characterised by severe wasting yet preserved serum albumin?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Kwashiorkor</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Kwashiorkor is dominated by protein deficiency. Albumin falls and oedema develops, often making the patient appear deceptively well-covered despite severe depletion.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Marasmus</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. In marasmus, chronic balanced starvation depletes energy and protein stores, but hepatic albumin synthesis is maintained. This is why a normal albumin must never be used to exclude malnutrition.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Marasmic-kwashiorkor</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Marasmic-kwashiorkor combines chronic wasting with hypoalbuminaemia and oedema — albumin is low in this mixed form, not preserved.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Sarcopenic obesity</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Sarcopenic obesity describes hidden muscle loss and micronutrient deficiency behind a high body weight. It is not defined by albumin status.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Review the spectrum: marasmus preserves albumin because hepatic synthesis continues despite whole-body wasting. Kwashiorkor and the mixed form both show low albumin."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. Preserved albumin in a wasted patient is the hallmark of marasmus — a key distinction from kwashiorkor."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
