          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Which consequence of surgical malnutrition creates a self-reinforcing cycle that</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which consequence of surgical malnutrition creates a self-reinforcing cycle that progressively worsens the nutritional deficit?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Impaired collagen synthesis causing wound dehiscence</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Impaired wound healing leads to dehiscence and anastomotic leak, but it does not directly deepen catabolism in a cyclical fashion.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Respiratory muscle wasting causing atelectasis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Diaphragm and intercostal wasting impairs coughing and ventilator weaning, but the primary self-reinforcing loop operates through a different mechanism.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Immune dysfunction leading to infection, which deepens catabolism</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Malnutrition depresses cell-mediated immunity, neutrophil function, and antibody production. The resulting infections trigger further catabolism through inflammatory mediators, worsening the deficit in a vicious cycle.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gut mucosal atrophy causing malabsorption</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Mucosal atrophy allows bacterial translocation and systemic sepsis, but the narration specifically identifies the infection–catabolism loop as the self-reinforcing cycle.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The key cycle is: malnutrition → immune failure → infection → deeper catabolism → worse malnutrition. Each turn amplifies the next."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Exactly. The infection–catabolism cycle is why malnourished surgical patients deteriorate rapidly once sepsis sets in."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
